  "verbalization": "The compound in question, (2S,3R,4S,5R,6S)-3,4,5-trihydroxy-6-[5-hydroxy-2-(4-hydroxyphenyl)-4-oxochromen-7-yl]oxyoxane-2-carboxylic acid, is implicated in the interaction with SNU-387 through multiple pathways. It is identified as a target of NRF2 activator Geopyxin F, which in turn targets SNU-387. Additionally, the compound acts as a target of DMS-273 and LNCaP, both of which are also targets of the same intermediate compound, 2-(2,6-Dihydroxyphenyl)-5-hydroxy-3,6,7-trimethoxychromen-4-one, which ultimately targets SNU-387. These findings suggest a complex network of interactions where the compound may influence SNU-387 through various molecular mechanisms, possibly involving the NRF2 signaling pathway and other cellular processes. The evidence supports a potential role for this compound in modulating SNU-387 activity, though the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated.",
